{"id": "4b927755-dc47-4ea1-af03-8f6994b65fc2", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T18:24:21.006689", "source": "user", "parent_id": "a5f2d097-9831-4f20-bf5a-8bd00616cded", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"This is a design-only task: produce a final experiment design (rationale, controls, analysis plan, feasibility) to answer whether OPRO-discovered optimized instructions outperform the baseline prompts ('Let's think step by step.' and the empty prompt) on BBH tasks. Execution is not required and should not be claimed. For this first turn, please provide: (1) a brief inspection of any relevant materials in /workspace that bear on the design (e.g., any references to OPRO procedure, BBH task suites, scoring conventions, prior instruction-optimization baselines); (2) a proposed design covering (a) which optimized instructions to test (e.g., the published OPRO leaders such as 'Take a deep breath' and 'Let's work this out in a step by step way to be sure we have the right answer'), (b) the task sampling strategy across BBH subtasks (full suite vs. representative subset, how many examples per subtask, train/val/test split discipline), (c) the scoring protocol (accuracy, average/aggregate, per-subtask breakdown, multiple-run aggregation, decoding settings), (d) the model and serving setup (which model family, temperature, context), (e) computational budget estimate; (3) an explicit list of assumptions and uncertainties that the design depends on. Do not run an experiment; do not fabricate results. Keep the response focused on inspection + proposed design + assumptions.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Do the optimized instructions discovered by OPRO outperform the baseline instructions ('Let's think step by step.' and the empty prompt) on BBH tasks?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
